areth was a Jewish rabbi.\",\"line\":3,\"span\":\"a Jewish rabbi\"},{\"text\":\"Jesus of Nazareth was crucified in Jerusalem around AD 30–33.\",\"line\":3,\"span\":\"who was crucified in Jerusalem around AD 30–33\"},{\"text\":\"The followers of Jesus of Nazareth proclaimed that he arose from the dead.\",\"line\":3,\"span\":\"whose followers proclaimed that he arose from the dead\"},{\"text\":\"Monotheism is a central belief of Christianity.\",\"line\":5,\"span\":\"Its central beliefs are monotheism\"},{\"text\":\"The Trinity (God as Father, Son, and Holy Spirit) is a central belief of Christianity.\",\"line\":5,\"span\":\"the Trinity (God as Father, Son, and Holy Spirit)\"},{\"text\":\"The incarnation and divinity of Jesus is a central belief of Christianity.\",\"line\":5,\"span\":\"the incarnation and divinity of Jesus\"},{\"text\":\"Salvation by God's grace through faith in Christ's death and resurrection is a central belief of Christianity.\",\"line\":5,\"span\":\"salvation by God's grace through faith in Christ's death and resurrection\"},{\"text\":\"The sacred text of Christianity is the Bible.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"Its sacred text is the Bible\"},{\"text\":\"The Bible is made up of the Old and New Testaments.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"made up of the Old and New Testaments\"},{\"text\":\"Christians regard the Bible as the inspired and authoritative Word of God.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"which Christians regard as the inspired and authoritative Word of God\"},{\"text\":\"Baptism as a rite of initiation is a core practice of Christianity.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"Core practices include baptism as a rite of initiation\"},{\"text\":\"The Eucharist (communion) is a core practice of Christianity.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"the Eucharist (communion) commemorating Jesus' last supper with his diciples\"},{\"text\":\"The Eucharist commemorates Jesus' last supper with his disciples.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"the Eucharist (communion) commemorating Jesus' last supper with his diciples\"},{\"text\":\"Prayer is a core practice of Christianity.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"prayer\"},{\"text\":\"Communal worship in a church is a core practice of Christianity.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"communal worship in a church\"},{\"text\":\"Over the centuries Christianity divided into three main branches: Catholicism, Eastern Orthodoxy, and Protestantism.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"Over the centuries the faith divided into three main branches — Catholicism, Eastern Orthodoxy (split in the East–West Schism of 1054), and Protestantism (emerging from the 16th-century Reformation)\"},{\"text\":\"Eastern Orthodoxy split in the East–West Schism of 1054.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"Eastern Orthodoxy (split in the East–West Schism of 1054)\"},{\"text\":\"Protestantism emerged from the 16th-century Reformation.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"Protestantism (emerging from the 16th-century Reformation)\"},{\"text\":\"Christianity is growing fastest in Africa and Asia today.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"today it is growing fastest in Africa and Asia\"},{\"text\":\"Christianity is declining in much of the West today.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"while declining in much of the West\"}]}","ttft_ms":9769,"type":"result","duration_ms":9791,"uuid":"5bbc36b4-967c-47de-ba1a-ab2a828eab32","ttft_stream_ms":1447,"time_to_request_ms":116,"first_content_frame_ms":1447,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
